!> Importance sampling against a multivariate Gaussian proposal N(mean, covariance) -- a natural choice
!> when a Laplace approximation is available and reasonably close to the target's shape (e.g.
!> bayes::MAP's mode paired with a numerically estimated Hessian there). Produces a weighted i.i.d.
!> sample in one shot rather than a Markov chain -- no warmup, nothing to check for mixing -- but
!> accuracy depends entirely on how well the Gaussian proposal covers the target's mass;
!> effective_sample_size is the diagnostic to check before trusting the result.
type, extends(rosetta_object), public :: ImportanceSampling
contains
    !> `log_target` need only be evaluable (optim::ArbitraryFunction), not differentiable.
    !> `proposal_covariance` (a plain d x d nested vector, not linalg::DenseMatrix -- matrices never cross
    !> the SWIG boundary as DenseMatrix anywhere in this library, only as nested vectors) must be symmetric
    !> positive definite.
    procedure :: sample => importancesampling_sample
    !> The options this ImportanceSampling was configured with.
    procedure :: options => importancesampling_options
end type

