!> The No-U-Turn Sampler (Hoffman & Gelman 2014, the efficient slice-sampling variant, Algorithm 3):
!> Hamiltonian Monte Carlo with an automatically chosen trajectory length -- the leapfrog trajectory is
!> grown by repeated doubling until it would start turning back on itself (a "U-turn"), removing the
!> need to hand-tune a fixed number of leapfrog steps. Step size is still adapted via the same
!> dual-averaging scheme as HMC. Uses an identity mass matrix.
type, extends(rosetta_object), public :: NUTS
contains
    !> Runs one chain: warmup with step-size adaptation, then num_samples draws.
    procedure :: sample => nuts_sample
    !> The options this NUTS was configured with.
    procedure :: options => nuts_options
end type

