!> Random-walk Metropolis-Hastings: the classic gradient-free MCMC baseline, proposing x' = x +
!> step_size * N(0, I) and accepting with probability min(1, exp(log_posterior(x') -
!> log_posterior(x))). Complements HMC/NUTS (which need a gradient via optim::DifferentiableFunction)
!> for targets where only a log-density evaluation is available -- a black-box model, a
!> discontinuous/non-differentiable posterior, or a director-subclassed optim::ArbitraryFunction in a
!> language without access to this library's autodiff.
type, extends(rosetta_object), public :: RandomWalkMetropolis
