!> Owned ordinary result and logical work, without retained cost-table history. Scratch consists of two
!> cost rows and one predecessor byte per positive cell. No input references survive return. Copies own
!> independent result paths.
!>
!> **Example**
!>
!> ```
!> const auto c=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_work({0,1},{0,1});
!> std::print("{} {}\n",c.result.distance,c.work.cells); // 0 4
!> ```
!>
!> See also: `dynamic_time_warping_work()`, `DTWTrace`.
