contains
    !> Gets C++ field `result`: Optimal path and its unnormalized absolute loss.
    procedure :: get_result => dtwcomputation_get_result
    !> Sets C++ field `result`: Optimal path and its unnormalized absolute loss.
    procedure :: set_result => dtwcomputation_set_result
    !> Gets C++ field `work`: Actual recurrence and traceback counts.
    procedure :: get_work => dtwcomputation_get_work
    !> Sets C++ field `work`: Actual recurrence and traceback counts.
    procedure :: set_work => dtwcomputation_set_work
end type

!> Owned input, actual accumulated costs and chosen predecessors from one DTW run. Positive cells are
!> row-major at i*b.size()+j; sentinel border is implicit. Costs and predecessor codes are captured
!> during the original recurrence, not reconstructed afterward. Infinite cells mark unrepresentable
!> costs. Logical capture entries are a.size()+b.size()+2*a.size()*b.size(): one per input scalar, cost
!> and direction. Result paths, rolling scratch rows, scalar metadata and allocator bytes are excluded.
!> Copies are independent.
!>
!> **Example**
!>
!> ```
!> const auto t=dm::geometry::dynamic_time_warping_trace({1},{4});
!> std::print("{} {}\n",t.cumulative[0],t.captured_entries); // 3 4
!> ```
!>
!> See also: `dynamic_time_warping_trace()`, `dtw_trace_entries()`.
