!> FISTA on the ProximalFunction callback interface. Classical t recurrence (1+sqrt(1+4*t^2))/2 and
!> extrapolated gradient points, followed by the supplied proximal map. Stops on successive
!> accepted-coordinate displacement. No adaptive restart, backtracking or monotonicity safeguard.
!> Supply the correct proximal dimensions and a rate at most 1/L for the standard convex bound. The
!> caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate
!> in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and
!> propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external
!> synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
!>
!> **Example**
!>
!> ```
!> const dm::optim::FISTA optimizer;
!> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 10000
!> ```
