!> LBFGS on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface. Limited-memory BFGS with weak-Wolfe
!> bracket/bisection search, descent fallback and positive-curvature pair retention. If the search
!> budget ends, a previous Armijo step can be used; if none was found, returns. Tests gradient norm or
!> absolute objective change. O(history_size*p) state; history_size must be positive. The caller
!> supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in
!> place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and
!> propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable objective across threads requires external
!> synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a uniform convergence certificate.
!>
!> **Example**
!>
!> ```
!> const dm::optim::LBFGS optimizer;
!> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 500
!> ```
!>
!> **References**
!>
!> - J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization, second edition,
!>   https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5. The implemented variant and stopping rules are
!> specified above.
!>
!> See also: `LBFGSOptions`, `trace_optimize()`.
type, extends(rosetta_object), public :: LBFGS
contains
    !> Run LBFGS from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Limited-memory BFGS with
    !> weak-Wolfe bracket/bisection search, descent fallback and positive-curvature pair retention. If the
    !> search budget ends, a previous Armijo step can be used; if none was found, returns. Tests gradient
    !> norm or absolute objective change. O(history_size*p) state; history_size must be positive.
    procedure :: optimize => lbfgs_optimize
    !> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
    procedure :: options => lbfgs_options
end type

