!> NesterovAcceleratedGradient on the DifferentiableFunction callback interface. Evaluates the gradient
!> at coordinates+momentum*velocity, then updates velocity and coordinates. Tests that look-ahead
!> gradient after the update. Fixed momentum and rate do not implement every strongly-convex
!> acceleration schedule. O(p) reset local state. The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent
!> callbacks. Inputs are borrowed; coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a
!> callback throws. Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a
!> mutable objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone is not a
!> uniform convergence certificate.
!>
!> **Example**
!>
!> ```
!> const dm::optim::NesterovAcceleratedGradient optimizer;
!> std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_iterations); // 10000
!> ```
!>
!> **References**
!>
!> - J. Nocedal and S. J. Wright (2006), Numerical Optimization, second edition,
!>   https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-387-40065-5. The implemented variant and stopping rules are
!> specified above.
!>
!> See also: `NesterovAcceleratedGradientOptions`, `trace_optimize()`.
type, extends(rosetta_object), public :: NesterovAcceleratedGradient
contains
    !> Run NesterovAcceleratedGradient from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
    !> Evaluates the gradient at coordinates+momentum*velocity, then updates velocity and coordinates.
    !> Tests that look-ahead gradient after the update. Fixed momentum and rate do not implement every
    !> strongly-convex acceleration schedule. O(p) reset local state.
    procedure :: optimize => nesterovacceleratedgradient_optimize
    !> Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.
    procedure :: options => nesterovacceleratedgradient_options
end type

