!> A Box-Jenkins seasonal ARIMA(p, d, q)(P, D, Q)_s model, fit to a single numeric series by
!> conditional sum of squares (CSS): the series is differenced (regular d times, then seasonal D times
!> with period s) to stationarity, the combined AR/MA polynomials (regular composed with seasonal, via
!> polynomial multiplication) are estimated by minimizing the conditional residual sum of squares with
!> DifferentialEvolution, and forecasts are produced by recursing the fitted difference equation
!> forward and re-integrating through the differencing steps.
!>
!> Setting seasonal_period == 0 (the default) reduces this to a plain, non-seasonal
!> ARIMA(p, d, q) model -- i.e. SARIMA is the general case, ARIMA the special case,
!> exactly as in R's arima()/statsmodels' SARIMAX().
!>
!> Note: CSS estimation approximates the exact Gaussian likelihood by conditioning
!> on the first max(p + P*s, q + Q*s) observations rather than filtering the full
!> series (e.g. via a Kalman filter); it is a standard, textbook ARIMA fitting
!> method (R's arima(method = "CSS")) but will differ slightly from exact-ML fits.
type, extends(rosetta_object), public :: ARIMA
contains
    !> The options the model was fit with.
    procedure :: options => arima_options
    !> Fitted non-seasonal AR coefficients
    procedure :: ar_coefficients => arima_ar_coefficients
    !> Fitted non-seasonal MA coefficients
    procedure :: ma_coefficients => arima_ma_coefficients
    !> Fitted seasonal AR coefficients
    procedure :: seasonal_ar_coefficients => arima_seasonal_ar_coefficients
    !> Fitted seasonal MA coefficients
    procedure :: seasonal_ma_coefficients => arima_seasonal_ma_coefficients
    !> Fitted mean of the differenced series.
    procedure :: mean => arima_mean
    !> Length of the input series.
    procedure :: observations => arima_observations
    !> Number of residuals that enter the sum of squares.
    procedure :: n_used => arima_n_used
    !> Innovation variance estimate.
    procedure :: sigma2 => arima_sigma2
    !> Gaussian log-likelihood at the CSS estimate, over n_used() residuals.
    procedure :: log_likelihood => arima_log_likelihood
    !> Akaike information criterion.
    procedure :: aic => arima_aic
    !> Bayesian information criterion.
    procedure :: bic => arima_bic
    !> One-step-ahead fitted values on the original scale, aligned to the input series (the first
    !> `observations() - n_used()` entries -- the presample points conditioned on by CSS -- are copies of
    !> the observed value, matching a residual of exactly zero there rather than an undefined value).
    procedure :: fitted_values => arima_fitted_values
    !> One-step-ahead residuals on the original scale (zero for the presample points).
    procedure :: residuals => arima_residuals
    !> Point forecasts for the next `horizon` periods, on the original scale.
    procedure :: forecast => arima_forecast
    !> AR coefficients of the stationary (differenced) model after multiplying the regular and seasonal
    !> polynomials,
    procedure :: expanded_ar_coefficients => arima_expanded_ar_coefficients
    !> MA coefficients
    procedure :: expanded_ma_coefficients => arima_expanded_ma_coefficients
    !> The first `count`
    procedure :: psi_weights => arima_psi_weights
    !> Point forecasts and their standard errors (from the psi-weight / MA(infinity) expansion of the full,
    !> non-stationary AR/MA representation of y), on the original scale.
    procedure :: forecast_with_intervals => arima_forecast_with_intervals
end type

