!> Solve the steady P1 system for -(p*u')'+q*u=f with endpoint boundary data. Follows FEM1D's
!> mesh/coefficient/finite-arithmetic/nonsingular-pivot preconditions. Uses three-point Gauss-Legendre
!> quadrature of f times each local basis, natural boundary terms and symmetric Dirichlet elimination,
!> then Thomas elimination. O(N) work/storage for N nodes; invokes the source three times per element.
!> No callback pointer is retained. Independent calls share no mutable state.
interface fem1d_solve
    module procedure fem1d_solve_1
end interface
public :: fem1d_solve

!> Solve the steady system using an owned named spatial source, without a director callback. Shares the
!> live-source solver and its mathematical/precondition/storage contracts. Sources: zero=0 (params
!> unused); constant=c ({1}); linear=m*x+c ({1,0}); polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty gives0);
!> sine=A*sin(w*x+phase) ({1,1,0}). Missing trailing parameters use those defaults; extra parameters
!> are ignored except polynomial, which uses all entries. Name matching is exact/case-sensitive.
interface fem1d_solve_builtin
    module procedure fem1d_solve_builtin_1
end interface
public :: fem1d_solve_builtin

!> Integrate u_t-(p*u')'+q*u=f with P1 space and actual backward-Euler time intervals. Shares FEM1D's
!> spatial/finite-arithmetic/nonzero-pivot preconditions. Source and boundary data represent a
!> time-independent model; the live callback is actually reevaluated three times per element at every
!> time advance, not cached. Stores initial u0 as supplied, then imposes boundary data at later solves.
!> Nominal step dt is shortened at t_end; actual positive time differences enter the mass term. Stops
!> once t_end is reached, avoiding a duplicate rounded last time even when ceil(t_end/dt) overestimates
!> the number of advances. O(S*N) work/output storage for S advances/N nodes, O(N) assembly
!> temporaries; no optional trace or quota. Backward Euler is unconditionally stable for the coercive
!> semidiscrete model, not a guarantee of arbitrary-step accuracy or finite arithmetic for arbitrary
!> parameters. Input arrays remain unchanged; callback exceptions/side effects/concurrent safety belong
!> to caller.
interface fem1d_solve_transient
    module procedure fem1d_solve_transient_1
end interface
public :: fem1d_solve_transient

!> Integrate the same backward-Euler model with a named source and no callback subclass. Uses the same
!> private source construction as solve_builtin() and the same actual time loop as solve_transient();
!> no second solver or per-language glue. Names/defaults: zero=0; constant=c ({1}); linear=m*x+c
!> ({1,0}); polynomial=sum(params[i]*x^i) (empty0); sine=A*sin(w*x+phase) ({1,1,0}). Extra entries
!> ignored except polynomial; exact case-sensitive names. Source objects are local and synchronous;
!> results own values, not callback aliases. All spatial/time/initial-state, complexity and stability
!> contracts follow solve_transient(); ordinary output has no optional history/quota.
interface fem1d_solve_transient_builtin
    module procedure fem1d_solve_transient_builtin_1
end interface
public :: fem1d_solve_transient_builtin

