!> Run ConjugateGradient from the supplied point using the configured finite budget. Nonlinear
!> Polak-Ribiere-plus directions with negative beta truncated to zero, periodic/descent restarts and an
!> Armijo line search. It is not linear CG with exact line minimisation and does not imply termination
!> in p steps. Returns when gradient/change/search conditions stop progress.
!>
!> **Example**
!>
!> ```
!> dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
!> dm::optim::ConjugateGradientOptions controls;controls.max_iterations=5;
!> std::vector<double> x{0,0};
!> const auto value=dm::optim::ConjugateGradient(controls).optimize(f,x);
!> std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true
!> ```
!>
