!> Otsu's method: the grayscale threshold (0-255) that maximizes the between-class variance of the
!> pixels it would split into "below" and "at-or-above" groups -- the standard automatic threshold
!> selection when a fixed threshold isn't known in advance. Pairs directly with image::threshold(img,
!> otsu_threshold(img)).
!>
!> @param img
recursive function otsu_threshold_1(img, status) result(rs_res)
    class(Image), intent(in) :: img
